{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And these are the names.</b> This vav is connected to what was said above: 'and Yosef saw to Ephraim the sons of thirty years' etc. <b>And these are the names</b> — Rashi interpreted: they are compared to stars, which He brings out by number and brings in by number, as it is said: 'who brings out by number their host' etc. And if you ask: where do we find that He brings them in by number? One may answer: from the fact that it says 'בשם יקרא' (He calls by name), which teaches that it speaks of bringing them in." "<b>And these are the names.</b> He counted them again to say that all of them came to Egypt and died there." "<b>Who come to Egypt.</b> It should have written 'who came.' But because of the cruelty that the Egyptians did to them after Yosef's death, they appeared to them every day as if they were just now arriving and had never seen them before." "<b>Et Yaakov.</b> With Yaakov." "<b>Each man and his house.</b> Each man and his wife, as it is written: 'apart from the wives of Yaakov's sons,' because Yaakov knew of them in Egypt that they were steeped in lust, and he feared lest his sons learn from their deeds, so he married them off before they went down to Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:43.448694924Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}